-- §11  Whether a fused supply still arrives in whole units, and where that question has no answer.
# One row per composed layer all of whose parts are lumpy: the largest whole unit that every part's
# quantum, converted into the composed layer's unit, is a whole number of, and a typed blank where
# there is none.
#
# The common whole unit
#   Each part's nameplate is a whole number of its own quanta, so any total the parts make is a
#   whole number of the common unit, and no larger unit holds for all of them. Not every such total
#   can be reached, because nobody holds a negative number of units: quanta of 4 and 6 never make
#   2.
#
# Two blanks, two facts
#   `unmeasured` where a part's conversion factor is: nobody sized it, so nobody can say what the
#   parts share. `notApplicable` where the converted quanta still sit in different units, a
#   question with no meaning rather than one left unanswered.
#
# `1` is a real answer
#   Not a failure. Every amount is a whole number of ones, so nothing is constrained, and the fused
#   supply is continuous as far as the arithmetic can see.
-- composition/composed_quantum.sqlc, ordered by whether the question has an answer.
SELECT c.composition                                   AS "composition!",
       c.composed_layer                                AS "composed_layer!",
       c.parts                                         AS "parts!",
       coalesce(c.unit, '(none)')                      AS "unit!",
       coalesce(c.composed_quantum::text || CASE WHEN c.spread THEN ' (at a factor''s mode)' ELSE '' END,
                '(' || c.absent || ')')                AS "quantum!"
FROM (
    :compose(composition/composed_quantum.sqlc)
) c
ORDER BY (c.absent IS NOT NULL) DESC, c.composition, c.composed_layer
